e to its high affinity for chromaffin cells,50\r\n11956,FEOCROMOCITOMA,SDHB,\"FEOCROMOCITOMA is associated with mutations in the SDHB gene, which are linked to hereditary forms of this tumor. These mutations indicate a genetic risk factor for the development of feocromocitomas, suggesting that individuals with such mutations may have an increased likelihood of developing this type of tumor.\",50\r\n11941,FEOCROMOCITOMA,ANTIDEPRESIVOS TRICÍCLICOS,\"FEOCROMOCITOMA, also known as pheochromocytoma, is a type of tumor that arises from the adrenal glands and can lead to the overproduction of catecholamines, resulting in various symptoms such as hypertension. Antidepresivos tricíclicos, or tricyclic antidepressants, are a class of medications used primarily to treat depression and certain anxiety disorders. However, these antidepressants can significantly affect the interpretation of diagnostic tests for pheochromocytoma. Specifically, they can interfere with the diagnostic process by impacting MIBG (metaiodobenzylguanidine) uptake, which is a crucial component in the imaging and diagnosis of pheochromocytomas. Therefore, the use of tricyclic antidepressants may complicate the accurate diagnosis of pheochromocytoma, necessitating careful consideration in clinical settings.\",49\r\n11936,FEOCROMOCITOMA,TUMORES SECRETORES DE CATECOLAMINAS,Pheochromocytoma is a specific type of tumor that secretes catecholamines,49\r\n11963,FEOCROMOCITOMA,SUPRARRENAL,\"Feocromocitomas are tumors that develop in the suprarrenal glands, leading to hypertension\",49\r\n11964,FEOCROMOCITOMA,TAC ABDOMINAL,TAC abdominal is performed to identify the presence of feocromocitomas in the adrenal glands,49\r\n11939,FEOCROMOCITOMA,CRESPO HERNÁNDEZ I,\"Crespo Hernández I is an author known for his contributions to the literature on pheochromocytomas, including a manual that discusses the condition and its management. His work provides valuable insights into the understanding and treatment of feocromocitomas, contributing to the broader medical knowledge surrounding this adrenal gland tumor.\",48\r\n11938,FEOCROMOCITOMA,DÍAZ PÉREZ JA,\"Díaz Pérez JA is an author known for his contributions to the literature on pheochromocytomas, including a manual that discusses the condition and its management. His work provides valuable insights into feocromocitomas, a type of tumor that affects the adrenal glands and can lead to significant health issues if not properly managed.\",48\r\n11950,FEOCROMOCITOMA,GEN VHL,\"Feocromocitoma, a type of tumor that arises from the adrenal glands, is often associated with mutations in the VHL gene. This genetic link suggests that individuals with mutations in the VHL gene have an increased risk of developing feochromocytomas, as well as other types of tumors. The relationship between feocromocitoma and the VHL gene underscores the importance of genetic factors in the development of this condition.\",48\r\n11957,FEOCROMOCITOMA,SDHC,\"Mutations in the SDHC gene are associated with feocromocitomas, contributing to the genetic understanding of these tumors\",48\r\n11959,FEOCROMOCITOMA,SDHD,\"The SDHD gene is associated with the risk of developing feocromocitomas, particularly in relation to hypoxia\",48\r\n3582,SENSIBILIDAD,FEOCROMOCITOMA,Sensitivity of tests like 18F-FDG is important for detecting metastatic feocromocitomas,48\r\n11965,FEOCROMOCITOMA,ANATOMOPATOLÓGICO,Anatomopathological reports are used to confirm the diagnosis of feocromocitomas,47\r\n11942,FEOCROMOCITOMA,CALCIOANTAGONISTAS,Calcioantagonistas can interfere with the diagnostic process for pheochromocytoma by affecting MIBG uptake,47\r\n11947,FEOCROMOCITOMA,CRISIS HIPERTENSIVAS,Feocromocitomas can cause crisis hipertensivas if not properly managed,47\r\n11935,FEOCROMOCITOMA,FENOXIBENZAMIDA,\"Fenoxibenzamida, also known as phenoxybenzamine, is utilized in the preoperative management of feocromocitomas (pheochromocytomas) to effectively control hypertensive episodes. This medication